-I checked the main target areas:
-- `src/investigators/hypothesis-types.ts`
-- `src/investigators/hypothesis-generator.ts`
-- `src/investigators/hypothesis-evidence-collector.ts`
-- `src/investigators/hypothesis-templates.ts`
-- `src/investigators/kubernetes-investigator.ts`
-- `src/investigators/seed-generator.ts`
-- `src/investigators/orchestrator.ts`
-- the corresponding existing test files
-
-The plan generally matches how this codebase is structured:
-- hypothesis generation is template-driven already, so threading `evidenceRules` through the `Hypothesis` object is the right seam
-- evidence collection is category-dispatched and has a real fallback gap for categories like `oom-kill`
-- node investigation already exists, so extending it for allocatable/capacity, taints, and node→pod correlation is incremental rather than architectural churn
-- cross-symptom correlation is already implemented and wired in, so adding orchestrator-level E2E coverage is appropriate
-- dedup really is concentrated in `orchestrator.ts`, so contract tests/docs there are the right place
-- calibration coverage belongs in `hypothesis-ranker.test.ts`, and the benchmark script exists as described
-- the documentation files named in the plan all exist
-
-Non-blocking suggestions:
-- In 7.11, be aware `collectEvidenceForHypothesis()` currently only gets `(hypothesis, context)`. `InvestigatorContext` does not carry source `Finding` objects or their titles, only bundle artifacts. So template-rule matching can definitely search logs/events/resources/symptom text, but “finding titles” would need either extra plumbing or a slight scope adjustment.
-- Also in 7.11, `missing-service` and `bad-db-endpoint` are valid categories but are not currently present in the template registry. If those are meant to be template-driven now, the implementation may need to add template entries or keep the tests focused on manually-constructed hypotheses / existing template categories.
-- For 7.10, the taint and MemoryPressure correlations should be easy to add, but the exact edge target may depend on whether the investigator links to event nodes or finding IDs; the tests should assert the intended contract, not overconstrain internal edge shape unless necessary.
-
-Verdict: approve
