OOMKilled evidence from container statuses and events (currently falls through to generic fallback).\\n2. Test that a `generic-crash` hypothesis uses template evidence rules to match error/panic/fatal patterns in logs.\\n3. Test that template-driven evidence collection produces supporting items matching rule patterns and contradicting items matching contradicting rule patterns.\\n\\n**Implementation:**\\n1. Add `evidenceRules?: EvidenceRule[]` field to the `Hypothesis` interface in `src/investigators/hypothesis-types.ts`.\\n2. In `src/investigators/hypothesis-generator.ts`, pass `evidenceRules` from the template definition through `buildHypothesis()` so they reach the `Hypothesis` object.\\n3. In `src/investigators/hypothesis-evidence-collector.ts`, add a new `collectTemplateRuleEvidence(hypothesis, context)` function that iterates over `hypothesis.evidenceRules`, compiles each rule's pattern into a RegExp, and searches logs + events + finding titles for matches. Supporting rules produce supporting evidence items; contradicting rules produce contradicting items.\\n4. In `collectEvidenceForHypothesis`, after the category-specific collector runs (or instead of the generic fallback), call `collectTemplateRuleEvidence` to augment the assessment with template-driven evidence. For categories WITH a dedicated collector (dns-failure, missing-secret, etc.), template rules act as a supplement. For categories WITHOUT a collector (oom-kill, generic-crash, bad-db-endpoint, missing-service), template rules ARE the primary evidence source.\\n5. Update the `CATEGORY_COLLECTORS` dispatch table comment to document the fallback chain: dedicated collector → template rules → generic fallback.\",\n  \"requiredChecks\": [\n    \"lint\",\n    \"typecheck\",\n    \"unit\",\n    \"build\"\n  ]\n}\n\nYou are the first agent to work on this step.\nImplement the changes described above, run checks to verify, and fix any issues before handing off.\nBe thorough — the next agent will review your work and should find it correct.\n\nWhen done, explain what you reviewed, what you changed (if anything), and your assessment.\n\nEnd with:\nVerdict: approve  — if the step is complete and correct, no more changes needed\nVerdict: changes_made  — if you made fixes or improvements\nVerdict: replan_needed  — if the step is structurally impossible to complete as planned and needs controller-managed replanning"}],"timestamp":1774099225866}}
